## Limitations

The questions come from templates over three warehouses, so the results describe this catalog and
these shapes; the template test set measures how far the checkpoint carries past them. The twins are
perturbations of the same tables and catch only answers that are right by accident on these values.
The base is small and the card is a T4, so the comparison between methods is at one modest budget.

## Monitoring

The share of answers each hack detector flags, on every held-out set:

{{ table(m ~ ".hacks") }}

During training the registered monitors (config/monitor.yaml) watch the same detectors on every
step; an alert on a defect arm stops it at its next checkpoint, and the gate above holds a checkpoint
whose run raised one in its last steps.

## Effective challenges on record

- Two billion parameters on templated questions is not a customer workload. Agreed, and the pages
  say so; the template test set is the honest measure of how far it carries.
- The reward could be gamed. The defect study plants four defects and two controls and shows which
  hacks each found, and every number here is twin confirmed, which the training reward never saw.
- One seed where the quota ran out. The seed spread gate says how many seeds stand behind the
  number.
